  "extraction_notes": "The stereochemistry in the generic schemes 1, 4, and 5 was interpreted as (S,S) based on the L-amino acid standard and consistent representation across the figure. In reaction 5na, the Boc-protected substrate is Boc-L-Proline. For 5ma, the trityl group (Tr) was placed on the tau-nitrogen of the histidine side chain, which is the standard position for Boc-His(Tr)-OH. 5 Å MS (molecular sieves) are treated as an additive reagent. Catalyst D structure is not provided in the figure."
